{\b Files/Folders in Dataset and Description of Files}\line
[1 - Codes] Contains example codes supporting different aspects of references [1-4].\line
       [a - Experimental Case Study on Smart Road Bridge] The purpose of this code is to use MLE method for weight estimation of some trucks on the smart road bridge in an experimental case study. This code is described in chapter 2 of the dissertation document [4]. It is suggested to read this chapter first before using this code. Open mainSmartRoadBridgeNORBWIM.mlx to start.\line
      [b - MP-NOR-BWIM] The purpose of this code is to perform two steps: 1) calibration using single truck passages and then 2) weight estimation in multiple-truck events. See the chapter 3 of the dissertation document [4] for details of the methodology and tests and truck characteristics. Open mainMPNORBWIM.mlx to start.\line
     [c - Damge indicator computation] The purpose of this code is to compute the damage indicator values for the 3-axle truck for single and multiple-truck events. The damage indicator is defined and utilized in Chapter 4 of the dissertation [4]. Open mainDamageIndicatorCalc.mlx to start.\line
     [d - RefIL computation and thresholds for single-truck events] The purpose of this code is to compute the reference influence lines (ILs) using standard IL method and threshold computation for single-truck events. A detailed explanation is provided in the dissertation chapter 4 [4] to show how to calculate the RefILs and thresholds. This instruction is only to accelerate the implementation of the code by future readers. Open mainRefIL_SingleEvents.mlx to start.\line
     [e - RefIL computation and thresholds for multiple-truck events] The purpose of this code is to compute the reference ILs using MP-IL method and threshold computation for multiple-truck events. A detailed explanation is provided in the dissertation chapter 4 [4] to show how to calculate the RefILs and thresholds. This instruction is only to accelerate the implementation of the code by future readers. Open mainRefIL_MultiEvents.mlx to start.\line
[2 - FE Model] Contains information related to finite element model used in studies [2] and [3]. The model simulates bridge strains in response to a truck passing event.\line
     [a - Model] CSI Bridge (proprietary software) Files for running both healthy and damaged bridge simulations\line
     [b - Data] Contains model-generated data (strains vs time) for various truck axel configurations.\line
